      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While cost efficiency is crucial, immediately cutting roles based solely on AI output can severely damage culture and limit your future adaptability. Instead of outright layoffs, consider restructuring roles to focus on AI oversight, auditing, and exception handling. You can justify retaining staff by framing them as \"AI effectiveness managers\" or \"process improvers,\" focusing their value on refining the technology rather than executing the old workflow. This phased approach allows you to capture cost savings incrementally while retaining institutional knowledge.",
      "source": "target",
